                <pb facs="1129" n="1121" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg1121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390D.11/164: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-09T13:00:00+02:00">December 9, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 9—8:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>63. Your telegram No. 29, December 7, noon. Foreign Office some weeks ago
                    requested for the proposed nationality arrangement approval of the Ministry of
                    the Interior which has full jurisdiction in the matter and it has now requested
                    that the decision be expedited. I understand that there seems to be no
                    opposition to the proposal and that the necessary bureaucratic action may
                    probably be taken within fortnight or so.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
